# copyfresh (scratch/orch/copyfresh-AUDIT.md): REJECTED at `bind F = H`.
# With F's poly A read as a fresh c_A in CopyOutputs (oracle: @copy),
# F's A.m is () -> c_A [U := c_A] and H's () -> A [U := A] (Y read at
# the site as go's A), so they differ. Before, sigma = [Y := TAbs A]
# alone made them equal (FamilyCopyRealizeOk was false,
# hunt2-family/REPORT.md in moss-safety). Original header:
# COUNTEREXAMPLE to FS.FamilyCopyRealizeOk (family copy, no platform code).
# This is the family instance of the hole hunt2-chain/t3-copy-bracket-nonfixed.moss
# found: BFunCopy's CopyOutputs sigma is built from F's FIXED readings only, and
# those readings may name one of F's poly symbols.
#   F[A]: A, Y, y0 -> A.m[U = A], A.k[U = Y]     X(F) = {Y}, P(F) = {A}
#   H[A]: A, Y, y0 -> A.m[U = Y], A.k[U = Y]     X(H) = {Y}
#   (.m/.k : () -> U, U a non-requirement type that sigclose puts in theta)
# In go (assume A), `bind Y = A` makes Y read TAbs A. sigma = [Y := TAbs A].
# Read at Cu_F, F's A.m is () -> A [U := A] and H's is () -> Y [U := Y];
# after sigma both are () -> A [U := A], so CopyOutputs holds (rm = [0,1]).
# Every other BFunCopy premise holds (Fixed H = Fixed F = {Y}; FixedAgreement;
# same needs y0 : Y; SameResult leaves (A,m),(A,k)). The copy-site A is go's
# outer A, but sigma identifies it with F's poly A.
# use_it (assume A, Y, y0, F) demands Concrete.m: matching A := Concrete,
# Cr gives Concrete.m : () -> Concrete. FamilyCopyRealizeOk's premises all
# hold (gfh Y = gfx Y = Bool). The application completes: G's body (via H's
# closure) has A := Concrete, Y := ground d (TAbs Y) = Bool, and installs,
# under the caller's key, A.m[U = Y] = () => y0 returning `true`. CallableOk
# at () -> Concrete fails; Audit's run is stuck at `match r { Concrete => () }`.
# Oracle (sigclose var build): rejects the copy, "effective output
# interpretation differs (D78)" (its copy_output_compatible replaces F's
# non-fixed generations by fresh @copy symbols). Native: "this construct is
# not supported by the compiler" at the demand. Audit: ACCEPTS (as argued).
# Control v3b (F's bracket U = Y, as H's): oracle 0, native 0.
type A;
type U;
type Y;
tag Concrete;
assume A { fn .m(): U; fn .k(): U; }
val y0: Y;
val a0: A;
functor F[A]: A, Y, y0 -> A.m[U = A], A.k[U = Y];
functor H[A]: A, Y, y0 -> A.m[U = Y], A.k[U = Y];
functor G: A, Y, y0 -> A.m[U = Y], A.k[U = Y] {
  bind A.m[U = Y] = () => y0;
  bind A.k[U = Y] = () => y0;
}
assume A, Y, y0, F {
  fn use_it() {
    let r: Concrete = Concrete.m();
    match r { Concrete => () };
  }
}
assume A, a0 {
  fn go() {
    bind Y = A;
    bind y0 = a0;
    bind H = G;
    bind F = H;
    use_it();
  }
}
fn main() {
  bind A = Bool;
  bind a0 = true;
  go();
}
